.TH EVENT_LOOP_SHUTDOWN 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
event_loop_shutdown \- stop an event loop's reactor thread
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t event_loop_shutdown(event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Signals loop's background reactor thread to stop and blocks until it has
been joined.  No dispatch can be in flight once this call returns.

Idempotent: safe to call more than once, including concurrently from
multiple threads.  Exactly one caller actually performs the join;
every other concurrent caller blocks until that join completes before
returning, so every caller's own "blocks until joined" contract holds
regardless of which one triggered the shutdown.

event_loop_destroy() calls this internally if the caller never called it
explicitly, so calling it directly first is optional; do so when the
"reactor thread stopped" and "resources freed" steps need to happen at
different times.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  event_loop to shut down.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        Shut down (or already was).
ccol_invalid_args   loop is NULL.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call concurrently from multiple threads other than loop's own
reactor thread.
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
Must not be called from within a callback running on loop's own reactor
thread.  This function joins that thread internally; a thread cannot
join itself (undefined behavior / EDEADLK).  Defer shutdown to another
thread, or to after the callback returns, instead.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_destroy (3),
.BR event_loop_create (3)
